A published build chooses nothing
================================

The engine's defaults were `active_provider: "ollama"` and `active_model: "qwen2.5-coder:32b"`. Both were
local, and local was the right instinct — but it is still the build deciding something for a person who
has not decided anything, and the first thing they see is a provider and a model they did not pick and
did not ask for. They are empty now. Empty means the app asks.

The published edition's label is `(volkdude85 published)` so the title bar says which of the two builds
is running, next to a developer build that says `(volkdude85 developer)`.

diff -ruN '--exclude=target' '--exclude=.git' '--exclude=*.orig' '--exclude=*.rej' a/crates/quixi-engine/src/providers.rs b/crates/quixi-engine/src/providers.rs
--- a/crates/quixi-engine/src/providers.rs	2026-11-02 23:03:15.214366943 -0800
+++ b/crates/quixi-engine/src/providers.rs	2026-11-02 23:07:11.112154258 -0800
@@ -922,11 +922,12 @@
 
         ProvidersStateFile {
             onboarding_completed: false,
-            // Local by default. Nothing leaves the machine until the person chooses otherwise, and a
-            // cloud provider with no key configured is a dead end on first run — which is exactly what
-            // a default should not be.
-            active_provider: "ollama".to_string(),
-            active_model: "qwen2.5-coder:32b".to_string(),
+            // Nothing selected, by design. A shipped build that opens on a provider and a model — even
+            // a local one — is a build that has decided something for a person who has not decided
+            // anything yet, and the first thing they see is a name they did not choose and cannot
+            // cancel. Empty means the app asks.
+            active_provider: String::new(),
+            active_model: String::new(),
             subagent_provider: String::new(),
             subagent_model: String::new(),
             providers,
diff -ruN '--exclude=target' '--exclude=.git' '--exclude=*.orig' '--exclude=*.rej' a/resources/edition.txt b/resources/edition.txt
--- a/resources/edition.txt	2026-11-02 23:03:15.150117861 -0800
+++ b/resources/edition.txt	2026-11-02 23:07:11.112975703 -0800
